--- !u!114 &1106618148
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1106618147}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a97f94a388714c045a9443c322611ab9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questions:
  - questionText: What is the main purpose of the "recognition rather than recall"
      heuristic?
    answers:
    - To require users to memorize steps for efficiency
    - To minimize the cognitive load by displaying relevant information
    - To make users type everything manually instead of selecting options
    - To improve password security by requiring memorization
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - questionText: Which heuristic is violated when a user interface uses jargon that
      is difficult to understand?
    answers:
    - Visibility of system status
    - Error prevention
    - Match between system and the real world
    - Aesthetic and minimalist design
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
  - questionText: Which of the following is an example of an accessibility feature
      that aligns with the "error recovery" heuristic?
    answers:
    - An undo button for accidental deletions
    - A complex CAPTCHA for security purposes
    - Disabling the back button to prevent navigation errors
    - Requiring users to re-enter data after an error
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - questionText: Why is keyboard accessibility important in web and application
      design?
    answers:
    - Some users rely on keyboard navigation due to mobility impairments
    - It improves the aesthetics of a website
    - It eliminates the need for screen readers
    - It makes websites load faster
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - questionText: What is an example of a "visibility of system status" heuristic
      in accessibility?
    answers:
    - Providing real-time feedback when a form is being processed
    - Hiding system messages to reduce screen clutter
    - Requiring users to refresh the page to check for updates
    - Removing progress bars to make the interface cleaner
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - questionText: Which principle of accessibility ensures that a website or application
      can be used with assistive technologies such as screen readers?
    answers:
    - Robust
    - Perceivable
    - Operable
    - Understandable
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - questionText: Which of the following is an example of "user control and freedom"
      in an accessible interface?
    answers:
    - Allowing users to easily cancel an action or go back
    - Locking users into a specific process with no way to exit
    - Removing back buttons to prevent errors
    - Automatically submitting forms without confirmation
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - questionText: What is an example of the "aesthetic and minimalist design" heuristic?
    answers:
    - Using complex animations on every page transition
    - Displaying only the essential information needed for a task
    - Filling the screen with as much content as possible
    - Using multiple pop-ups to provide extra information
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - questionText: Why is alternative text (alt text) important for images?
    answers:
    - It helps with website loading speeds
    - It provides descriptions for visually impaired users using screen readers
    - It prevents images from displaying incorrectly
    - It only helps with SEO rankings
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - questionText: Which of the following is NOT a key consideration when designing
      for cognitive disabilities?
    answers:
    - Using clear and simple language
    - Providing multiple ways to complete tasks
    - Requiring fast reaction times for key actions
    - Avoiding distractions and unnecessary animations
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
  - questionText: Which heuristic is violated if an application frequently crashes
      without warning or explanation?
    answers:
    - Error prevention
    - Help and documentation
    - Visibility of system status
    - Flexibility and efficiency of use
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
  - questionText: Why should websites provide captions for videos?
    answers:
    - To improve video resolution
    - To make videos accessible to users who are hard of hearing
    - To make videos accessible to users who are deaf
    - To make the page load faster
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - questionText: Which WCAG principle ensures that content can be understood by
      a wide range of users?
    answers:
    - Robust
    - Understandable
    - Operable
    - Perceivable
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - questionText: What is the main purpose of the "help and documentation" heuristic?
    answers:
    - To eliminate the need for user guidance
    - To provide users with information to assist in completing tasks when needed
    - To force users to learn by trial and error
    - To remove tooltips and support pages for a minimalist design
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - questionText: Why is it important for a website to have sufficient color contrast?
    answers:
    - To make the website look more visually appealing
    - To improve visibility for users with color blindness or low vision
    - To match modern design trends
    - 'To reduce screen brightness and save battery life '
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
